The blend modes (cpp/src/blend.cpp), the adjustment layers (cpp/src/adjust.cpp)
and Select and Mask (cpp/src/refine.cpp) are ported from PhotoCraft,
https://github.com/storytold/photocraft (crates/color/src/blend.rs,
crates/compose/src/psblend.rs, crates/compose/src/adjust*.rs,
crates/doc/src/adjust.rs and crates/algo/src/matting.rs), licensed
MIT OR Apache-2.0.
Copyright (c) the PhotoCraft contributors.

The tool strip (cpp/src/toolbar.cpp) follows PhotoCraft's toolbar
(crates/ui-egui/src/panels/toolbar.rs: its sections, slots, flyouts and keys).
Its icons (cpp/assets/icons) are PhotoCraft's: Lucide icons (ISC, Lucide Icons
and Contributors, https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide; licence in
cpp/assets/icons/LICENSE-lucide.txt) and PhotoCraft's own (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Third-party code built into LayerTack:
- Dear ImGui (MIT), https://github.com/ocornut/imgui
- SDL2 (zlib), https://www.libsdl.org
- stb_image, stb_image_write (MIT / public domain), https://github.com/nothings/stb
- nanosvg (zlib), https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg, draws the tool icons
- ONNX Runtime (MIT), https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime, loaded at run time
- U2-Net-p (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/xuebinqin/U-2-Net, downloaded on first use of Select Subject
